<title>ITALY: Alitalia to sue farmers for damages.</title>
<headline>Alitalia to sue farmers for damages.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's national carrier Alitalia said on Monday it would sue dairy farmers for damages caused by protesters who blocked airports last week.</p>
<p>The national carrier said in a statement that it had lost billions of lire (millions of dollars) because of flight delays and cancellations.</p>
<p>Milan's main Linate airport had to be shut briefly last week because farmers in tractors had barricaded the access routes. Before the airport was shut, passengers had to walk the last three kilometres to the terminal.</p>
<p>Protests were also staged at Verona and Venice airports.</p>
<p>Alitalia said it had made the decision in order to protect its interests and wanted passengers to know it would not tolerate future protests.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi met dairy farmers on Monday to try to resolve the dispute over tough EU fines for milk overproduction.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
